# RONI — environment variables
#
# M1 does not use any of these yet. The app runs entirely on local,
# in-memory sample data. This file exists so the shape of future
# configuration is documented in the repo without ever committing a
# real value. Copy this file to `.env.local` (already git-ignored) and
# fill it in only when a later milestone actually wires the service up.

# --- Supabase (M3.0 — infrastructure only, no UI wired up yet) ---
# Both are safe to expose to the browser: NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL is
# just your project's URL, and the publishable key (Supabase's newer
# replacement for the old "anon key") carries no special privilege —
# Row Level Security decides what it can actually read or write. Never
# put a Supabase *secret* key (sb_secret_..., formerly "service_role")
# in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable — M3.0 doesn't use one at all.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- AI / Ask Roni (planned, not yet integrated) ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=                # server-only, never expose to the client

# --- Insurance data partners (planned, not yet integrated) ---
# BINDABLE_API_KEY=
# BINDABLE_REF_CODE=

# --- CMS Marketplace API (Health, M2.5) ---
# Server-only. Never prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — it must never
# reach the browser. See src/lib/services/cms/client.ts.
CMS_MARKETPLACE_API_KEY=
